Z||000000||Philphine||06-06-2001||10:09 AM||||<BR>i noticed in another thread you mentioned a brake conversion kit. would it happen to change the bolt pattern. i'm supposed to start collecting up 6000 pieces for a swap but if your kit dose that it might be worth waiting and getting some cash together for. i need to switch to 5x4.5".   ||||reg||1
Z||000001||The Fieromaster||06-06-2001||02:05 PM||||Our brake conversion kits use standard 5x100 bolt pattern... Im asuming your wanting to size up a bit?  The thing is our kits still use the Fiero hubs and for the front we supply the hub to you.  Then we use a standard Beretta/Grand Am rotor to slide over it.  Changing bol patterns would mean that I would have to find a different rotor that would fit correctly and still meet the caliper in the right place... Then find a hub that would mate to the Fiero but have a different bolt pattern!  Ouch lotta work 4 us! hehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  So the best thing (but perhaps not the safest) is to use a piece of steel that bolts to the Fiero brakes at 5x100 and then your wheel bolts to IT at whatever pattern you need.... Although If you use top grade bolts and tool steel or somthing perhaps as strong (but a bit lighter cause tool steel is HEAVY) you should be ok!<P>Woa  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> I typed allot!  I hope i didnt loose you!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">   <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
